IMPORT prelude

-- Higher Education Support Act 2003 (Cth) -- who is a Commonwealth supported student (ss 36-5, 36-10), entitlement to HECS-HELP
-- (ss 90-1, 90-5) and its amount (ss 93-1, 93-10, 93-20), entitlement to FEE-HELP (ss 104-1, 104-5) and the FEE-HELP loan fee
-- (s 137-10(2)), the HELP balance and loan limit (ss 128-15, 128-20), the 20% cut to HELP debts (ss 137-19A, 140-26), the
-- accumulated HELP debt and its indexation (ss 140-5, 140-10, 140-25, 140-30), and compulsory repayment through the tax system
-- (ss 154-1, 154-5, 154-10, 154-15, 154-20).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 104, compilation date 1 July 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 17, 2025), register id
-- C2026C00297, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A01234.txt. THE DEPOSIT DROPS THE FORMULAS THAT THE
-- REGISTER PRINTS AS IMAGES: the formulas in ss 93-5(1), 140-25(1), 140-26(2) and 154-25(2) are absent from the .txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0016 in subjects/au/requirements.jsonl (priority 1), raised 5 times by the three Western
-- Australian cradle-to-grave scenarios: Chloe c030 (2021-02-22, Bachelor of Commerce at UWA on HECS-HELP: what is deferred, and
-- when must she repay?), c045 (2024-10-20, first return for 2023-24 on $27,500: no HECS repayment under the threshold, s 154-10),
-- c048 (2025-10-25, second return for 2024-25 on $71,500: the compulsory repayment, ss 154-1 to 154-20); Daniel d020 (2014-02-24,
-- Bachelor of Commerce at UWA on HECS-HELP: what is deferred?), d022 (2017-02-27, Juris Doctor at UWA on FEE-HELP: is a
-- postgraduate law degree Commonwealth-supported? Parts 2-2, 3-3). SCOPED to the provisions those events name -- Parts 3-2, 3-3
-- and 4-2 and the Commonwealth supported student test in Part 2-2 -- with the definitions, conditions and exceptions needed to
-- answer them, and the Part 4-1 debt rules that carry a HELP loan into the repayment.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The allocation of places and the grant amounts (Divisions 30, 33) beyond what the CSP test needs; the Student
-- Learning Entitlement itself (an INPUT); the s 36-10(6), (7) and s 36-12 bars (one INPUT flag); the NZ special category test
-- (ss 90-5(2A), 104-5(2A), an INPUT); grandfathered student contribution amounts; the student contribution amount itself (set by
-- the provider under s 19-87 within the maximum -- an INPUT); indexation of the maximum contribution amounts and of the HELP loan
-- limit under Part 5-6 (the current-year figures are INPUTS; the figures below are the ones the text states); the CPI and WPI
-- index numbers (INPUTS); the replacement thresholds under s 154-25 for income years after 2025-26 (INPUTS); the s 140-26(2)
-- substituted formula (not in the deposit); re-crediting (Divisions 97, Subdivision 104-B); OS-HELP, SA-HELP, STARTUP-HELP,
-- VET FEE-HELP; overseas debtors (ss 154-16 to 154-32); location-preferred debtors (Divisions 142, 144); assessments and PAYG;
-- Medicare levy (s 8 of the Medicare Levy Act 1986, not deposited -- an INPUT); the meaning of taxable income, reportable fringe
-- benefits and the other s 154-5 components (INPUTS); and every earlier text of the Act. THIS IS THE 2026 TEXT: Daniel's 2014 and
-- 2017 enrolments, and Chloe's 2024-25 repayment, were governed by earlier texts that are not deposited.
--
-- Dates are written YYYYMMDD as numbers. An income year is named by the year in which it starts (2025 for 2025-26).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Higher Education Support Act 2003 -- HELP loans and their repayment`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- The facts about one student's enrolment in one unit of study.
DECLARE Enrolment HAS
    `Australian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `NZ citizen or permanent visa holder resident for the unit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `humanitarian or Pacific engagement visa holder resident for the unit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets the NZ special category test` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provider expects no units in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provider has a funding agreement for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Table A provider` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unit is within a funded national priority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unit contributes to the course` IS A BOOLEAN
    `assessed as academically suited` IS A BOOLEAN
    `unit is covered by the Student Learning Entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `FEE-FREE Uni Ready course` IS A BOOLEAN
    `enrolled at the end of the census date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `commenced the course on or after 1 January 2021` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has and notified a student identifier` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another s 36-10 or 36-12 bar applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `advised in writing of Commonwealth support` IS A BOOLEAN
    `opted out in writing by the census date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Secretary determined not a genuine student` IS A BOOLEAN
    `accredited course` IS A BOOLEAN
    `census date` IS A NUMBER
    `HELP balance` IS A NUMBER
    `meets the tax file number requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gave a request for Commonwealth assistance by the census date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `course is primarily at an overseas campus` IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets the FEE-HELP course requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a bar in s 104-1(3), (4) or 104-1AA applies` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `ss 36-5, 36-10 -- Commonwealth supported students`

-- s 36-10(1)(f), mirrored in s 104-1(1)(ga): the student identifier requirements apply "if: (i) the census date for the unit is
-- on or after 1 January 2021 and before 1 January 2023 and the person commenced the course of study on or after 1 January 2021;
-- or (ii) the census date for the unit is on or after 1 January 2023". (2C): the person has a student identifier immediately
-- before the census date and, before it, notifies it to the provider and the Secretary.
GIVEN `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the student identifier requirements apply` IF
        (    `the enrolment`'s `census date` AT LEAST 20210101
         AND `the enrolment`'s `census date` LESS THAN 20230101
         AND `the enrolment`'s `commenced the course on or after 1 January 2021`)
    OR  `the enrolment`'s `census date` AT LEAST 20230101

GIVEN `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the student identifier condition` IF
    (NOT `the student identifier requirements apply` `the enrolment`) OR `the enrolment`'s `has and notified a student identifier`

-- s 36-10(2): for paragraph (1)(c) the person must be "(a) an Australian citizen; or (b) a citizen of New Zealand who will be
-- resident within Australia for the duration of the unit; or (c) a permanent visa holder who will be resident within Australia
-- for the duration of the unit". (2B): not if the provider "reasonably expects that he or she will not undertake in Australia any
-- units of study contributing to the course of study".
GIVEN `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the s 36-10 citizenship or residency requirements` IF
        (`the enrolment`'s `Australian citizen` OR `the enrolment`'s `NZ citizen or permanent visa holder resident for the unit`)
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `provider expects no units in Australia`)

-- s 36-10(1): "A higher education provider must not advise a person that he or she is a Commonwealth supported student in
-- relation to a unit of study unless: (a) the provider has entered into a funding agreement under section 30-25 for the year
-- ...; (b) the unit contributes to the requirements of a course of study in which the person is enrolled ...; (ba) the person
-- has been assessed ... as academically suited to undertake the unit; (c) the person meets the citizenship or residency
-- requirements ...; (d) if the course of study is a course of study other than a FEE-FREE Uni Ready course -- the unit is covered
-- by the person's Student Learning Entitlement; (e) the person enrolled in the unit on or before the census date ... and ...
-- remained so enrolled; (f) [student identifier]". (3): nor if the person has notified that he or she does not wish to be
-- Commonwealth supported. (5): a provider that is not a Table A provider must not, unless the unit is within a national priority
-- for which it has received a grant. (6), (7) and s 36-12: further bars (one INPUT flag here).
GIVEN `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provider may advise Commonwealth support` IF
        `the enrolment`'s `provider has a funding agreement for the year`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `unit contributes to the course`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `assessed as academically suited`
    AND `meets the s 36-10 citizenship or residency requirements` `the enrolment`
    AND (`the enrolment`'s `FEE-FREE Uni Ready course` OR `the enrolment`'s `unit is covered by the Student Learning Entitlement`)
    AND `the enrolment`'s `enrolled at the end of the census date`
    AND `meets the student identifier condition` `the enrolment`
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `opted out in writing by the census date`)
    AND (`the enrolment`'s `Table A provider` OR `the enrolment`'s `unit is within a funded national priority`)
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `another s 36-10 or 36-12 bar applies`)

-- s 36-5(1): a person is a Commonwealth supported student in relation to a unit if "(a) the higher education provider ... has
-- advised the person in writing that he or she is a Commonwealth supported student ...; and (b) at the end of the census date
-- for the unit, the higher education provider would not have been prohibited under this Subdivision from so advising the person".
-- (3): "However, the person is not a Commonwealth supported student ... if he or she notifies ... that he or she does not wish to
-- be"; (5): nor if "the Secretary determines that the person is not a genuine student in relation to the unit".
-- Whether a postgraduate course carries Commonwealth supported places is not answered by the Act: it turns on the provider's
-- advice and funding agreement (s 36-10(1)(a)) and, for a Table A provider, on the Minister's allocation of places for
-- designated higher education courses (ss 30-10, 30-12) -- all INPUTS here.
GIVEN `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Commonwealth supported student` IF
        `the enrolment`'s `advised in writing of Commonwealth support`
    AND `the provider may advise Commonwealth support` `the enrolment`
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `opted out in writing by the census date`)
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `Secretary determined not a genuine student`)

§§ `ss 90-1, 90-5 -- entitlement to HECS-HELP`

-- s 90-5(1): "(a) the student is an Australian citizen; or (b) the student: (i) is a permanent humanitarian visa holder, an
-- eligible former permanent humanitarian visa holder or a Pacific engagement visa holder; and (ii) will be resident in Australia
-- for the duration of the unit". (2A): certain New Zealand citizens on a special category visa (an INPUT). (3): not if the
-- provider reasonably expects no units in Australia. An ordinary permanent visa holder, who may be Commonwealth supported under
-- s 36-10(2)(c), is NOT in this list.
GIVEN `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the HECS-HELP citizenship or residency requirements` IF
        (    `the enrolment`'s `Australian citizen`
          OR `the enrolment`'s `humanitarian or Pacific engagement visa holder resident for the unit`
          OR `the enrolment`'s `meets the NZ special category test`)
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `provider expects no units in Australia`)

-- s 90-1: "A student is entitled to HECS-HELP assistance for a unit of study ... if: (aa) the course of study is an accredited
-- course ...; (a) the student meets the citizenship or residency requirements under section 90-5; (b) the census date for the unit
-- is on or after 1 January 2005; (ba) the student's HELP balance is greater than zero; (c) the student is a Commonwealth supported
-- student in relation to the unit; (e) the student (i) enrolled in the unit on or before the census date ... and (ii) at the end of
-- the census date, remained so enrolled; (f) the student meets the tax file number requirements ...; (g) the student has, on or
-- before the census date, completed, signed and given ... a request for Commonwealth assistance".
GIVEN `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is entitled to HECS-HELP assistance` IF
        `the enrolment`'s `accredited course`
    AND `meets the HECS-HELP citizenship or residency requirements` `the enrolment`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `census date` AT LEAST 20050101
    AND `the enrolment`'s `HELP balance` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `is a Commonwealth supported student` `the enrolment`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `enrolled at the end of the census date`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `meets the tax file number requirements`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `gave a request for Commonwealth assistance by the census date`

§§ `ss 93-1, 93-10, 93-20, 96-1 -- what is deferred`

-- s 93-1: the amount of HECS-HELP assistance for a unit "is the difference between: (a) his or her student contribution amount
-- for the unit; and (b) the sum of any up-front payments made in relation to the unit". s 93-20(1): if it would exceed the HELP
-- balance on the census date (and no other unit shares the census date), it is "an amount equal to the student's HELP balance".
-- s 96-1: the Commonwealth must "(a) as a benefit to the student, lend to the student the amount of HECS-HELP assistance; and
-- (b) pay to the provider the amount lent in discharge of the student's liability to pay his or her student contribution amount".
GIVEN `student contribution amount` IS A NUMBER, `up-front payments` IS A NUMBER, `balance on the census date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the HECS-HELP assistance for the unit` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the greater of` 0 (`student contribution amount` MINUS `up-front payments`)) `balance on the census date`

-- s 93-20(2): if the HECS-HELP, FEE-HELP and VET FEE-HELP amounts for all units with the same census date "would exceed the
-- student's HELP balance on the census date ..., the total amount ... is an amount equal to that HELP balance". The Act's example:
-- Kate, a HELP balance of $2,000, four units at $600 each -- $2,000.
GIVEN `sum of the amounts for units with that census date` IS A NUMBER, `balance on the census date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total HELP assistance for units with one census date` MEANS
    `the lesser of` `sum of the amounts for units with that census date` `balance on the census date`

-- s 93-10 table, "The amount in respect of a non-grandfathered student". Note 2: "Maximum student contribution amounts for places
-- are indexed under Part 5-6" -- so these are the figures the text states, not the figure for any particular year.
DECLARE Discipline IS ONE OF
    `law, accounting, administration, economics or commerce`
    `communications or society and culture`
    `education, clinical psychology, English, mathematics or statistics`
    `allied or other health, built environment, computing, visual and performing arts, professional pathway psychology or social work`
    `nursing or Indigenous and foreign languages`
    `engineering, surveying, environmental studies or science`
    `agriculture`
    `medicine, dentistry or veterinary science`
    `pathology`

GIVEN `the discipline` IS A Discipline
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the stated maximum student contribution for a place` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the discipline`
    WHEN `law, accounting, administration, economics or commerce` THEN 14500
    WHEN `communications or society and culture` THEN 14500
    WHEN `education, clinical psychology, English, mathematics or statistics` THEN 3950
    WHEN `allied or other health, built environment, computing, visual and performing arts, professional pathway psychology or social work` THEN 7950
    WHEN `nursing or Indigenous and foreign languages` THEN 3950
    WHEN `engineering, surveying, environmental studies or science` THEN 7950
    WHEN `agriculture` THEN 3950
    WHEN `medicine, dentistry or veterinary science` THEN 11300
    WHEN `pathology` THEN 7950

§§ `ss 128-15, 128-20 -- the HELP balance`

-- s 128-20(1): "The HELP loan limit is: (a) $106,319; or (b) in relation to a person who is enrolled in a course of study in
-- medicine, ... dentistry, ... veterinary science or ... aviation, while the person is enrolled in that course -- $152,700."
-- Note: "The HELP loan limit is indexed under Part 5-6." (The current-year limit is an INPUT to the balance below.)
GIVEN `enrolled in medicine, dentistry, veterinary science or aviation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the stated HELP loan limit` MEANS
    IF `enrolled in medicine, dentistry, veterinary science or aviation` THEN 152700 ELSE 106319

-- s 128-15(1): the HELP balance is (a) if the HELP loan limit "exceeds the sum of all of the amounts of" HECS-HELP, FEE-HELP,
-- VET FEE-HELP and VET student loans "previously payable for the person", that sum "as reduced by any amounts previously
-- re-credited" -- "that excess"; (b) "otherwise -- zero". (2): "it is immaterial whether amounts ... have been repaid."
GIVEN `HELP loan limit` IS A NUMBER, `assistance previously payable` IS A NUMBER, `amounts re-credited` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the HELP balance` MEANS
    `the greater of` 0 (`HELP loan limit` MINUS (`assistance previously payable` MINUS `amounts re-credited`))

§§ `ss 104-1, 104-5 -- entitlement to FEE-HELP`

-- s 104-5(1): (a) Australian citizen; (b) permanent humanitarian, eligible former permanent humanitarian or Pacific engagement
-- visa holder resident for the unit; (c) [bridging courses for overseas-trained professionals -- not encoded]; (2A) certain New
-- Zealand citizens (an INPUT); (3) not if the provider expects no units in Australia.
GIVEN `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the FEE-HELP citizenship or residency requirements` IF
        (    `the enrolment`'s `Australian citizen`
          OR `the enrolment`'s `humanitarian or Pacific engagement visa holder resident for the unit`
          OR `the enrolment`'s `meets the NZ special category test`)
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `provider expects no units in Australia`)

-- s 104-1(1): entitled if "(a) the student meets the citizenship or residency requirements under section 104-5; (ac) the student
-- has been assessed ... as academically suited ...; (b) the student's HELP balance is greater than zero; (c) the census date ...
-- is on or after 1 January 2005; (d) the student is NOT a Commonwealth supported student in relation to the unit; (e) the unit meets
-- the course requirements under section 104-10; (f) [part of a course of study]; (g) [enrolled at the census date]; (ga) [student
-- identifier]; (h) [tax file number]; (i) [request for Commonwealth assistance]". (1AA): not if the Secretary determines the
-- student "is not a genuine student"; (2): not if the course is "undertaken by the student primarily at an overseas campus";
-- (3), (4) and s 104-1AA: provider limits, a provider completing the student's part of the request, and an unreasonable study
-- load (one INPUT flag).
GIVEN `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is entitled to FEE-HELP assistance` IF
        `meets the FEE-HELP citizenship or residency requirements` `the enrolment`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `assessed as academically suited`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `HELP balance` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the enrolment`'s `census date` AT LEAST 20050101
    AND (NOT `is a Commonwealth supported student` `the enrolment`)
    AND `the enrolment`'s `meets the FEE-HELP course requirements`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `enrolled at the end of the census date`
    AND `meets the student identifier condition` `the enrolment`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `meets the tax file number requirements`
    AND `the enrolment`'s `gave a request for Commonwealth assistance by the census date`
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `Secretary determined not a genuine student`)
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `course is primarily at an overseas campus`)
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `a bar in s 104-1(3), (4) or 104-1AA applies`)

§§ `ss 137-5, 137-10, 137-19A -- the HELP debt`

-- s 137-5(2): "The amount of the HECS-HELP debt is the amount of the loan." (3): it "is taken to have been incurred by a person
-- immediately after the census date for the unit". s 137-10(2): the FEE-HELP debt is "(a) if the loan relates to FEE-HELP
-- assistance for a unit of study provided by a Table B provider -- the amount of the loan; or (b) if paragraph (a) does not apply
-- and the loan relates to FEE-HELP assistance for a unit of study that forms part of an undergraduate course of study: (i) for a
-- unit of study with a census date between 1 April 2020 and 31 December 2022 -- the amount of the loan; or (ia) for a unit of study
-- with a census date on or after 1 January 2023 -- an amount equal to 120% of the loan; or (ii) otherwise -- an amount equal to
-- 125% of the loan; or (c) if neither paragraph (a) nor (b) applies -- the amount of the loan."
GIVEN `loan` IS A NUMBER, `Table B unit` IS A BOOLEAN, `undergraduate unit` IS A BOOLEAN, `the census day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the FEE-HELP debt before s 137-19A` MEANS
    IF `Table B unit` OR (NOT `undergraduate unit`) THEN `loan`
    ELSE IF `the census day` AT LEAST 20200401 AND `the census day` AT MOST 20221231 THEN `loan`
         ELSE IF `the census day` AT LEAST 20230101 THEN `loan` TIMES 120 DIVIDED BY 100
              ELSE `loan` TIMES 125 DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 137-19A: "(1) This section applies if ... a person incurs a HELP debt during the period beginning on 1 January 2025 and ending
-- on 1 June 2025. (2) ... the amount of the HELP debt is the amount worked out under that section reduced by 20%."
-- INFERENCE: a HECS-HELP or FEE-HELP debt is incurred "immediately after the census date" (ss 137-5(3), 137-10(3)), read here as
-- the day after it -- so a census date of 31 December 2024 falls inside the window and one of 1 June 2025 falls outside it.
GIVEN `the census day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a debt for the unit is incurred in the s 137-19A window` IF
    `the census day` AT LEAST 20241231 AND `the census day` AT MOST 20250531

GIVEN `debt before the reduction` IS A NUMBER, `the census day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the HELP debt for the unit` MEANS
    IF `a debt for the unit is incurred in the s 137-19A window` `the census day`
    THEN `debt before the reduction` TIMES 80 DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE `debt before the reduction`

§§ `ss 140-5, 140-10, 140-25, 140-26, 140-30 -- the accumulated HELP debt`

-- s 140-10(1)(b): the HELP debt indexation factor for 1 June is "the lower of the CPI indexation factor ... and the WPI
-- indexation factor", each a ratio of four quarters' index numbers "rounded to 3 decimal places" (INPUTS, already rounded).
GIVEN `CPI indexation factor` IS A NUMBER, `WPI indexation factor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the HELP debt indexation factor` MEANS
    `the lesser of` `CPI indexation factor` `WPI indexation factor`

-- s 140-5(1): the former accumulated HELP debt is the method statement amount multiplied by the HELP debt indexation factor.
-- Step 1: the previous accumulated HELP debt; Steps 2-2C: add the HELP debts incurred in the last 6 months of the preceding
-- financial year; Step 3: subtract voluntary repayments; Step 4: subtract compulsory repayment amounts assessed; Step 5:
-- subtract increases by amended assessment; Step 6: add reductions by amended assessment. s 140-26(1): for the accumulated HELP
-- debt for the financial year starting on 1 July 2024 add "Step 7. Reduce the amount worked out under step 6 by 20%."
-- The Act's example: Lorraine, $15,000 + $1,500 - $525 - $3,000, at a factor of 1.030.
GIVEN `previous accumulated HELP debt` IS A NUMBER, `HELP debts in the last 6 months` IS A NUMBER,
      `voluntary repayments` IS A NUMBER, `compulsory repayments assessed` IS A NUMBER,
      `increases by amendment` IS A NUMBER, `reductions by amendment` IS A NUMBER,
      `indexation factor` IS A NUMBER, `the financial year starts on 1 July 2024` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the former accumulated HELP debt` MEANS
    (`previous accumulated HELP debt` PLUS `HELP debts in the last 6 months` MINUS `voluntary repayments`
        MINUS `compulsory repayments assessed` MINUS `increases by amendment` PLUS `reductions by amendment`)
    TIMES (IF `the financial year starts on 1 July 2024` THEN 80 DIVIDED BY 100 ELSE 1)
    TIMES `indexation factor`

-- s 140-25(1): THE FORMULA IS NOT IN THE DEPOSIT. Its terms are defined: "former accumulated HELP debt", "HELP debt repayments"
-- (voluntary repayments of the HELP debts incurred in the year), "HELP debts incurred" (those incurred in the first 6 months of
-- the financial year, s 140-25(1A)) and "location-preferred HELP debtor reduction". INFERENCE, from the outline in s 140-1(3) and
-- the Act's example (Paula: $20,000 + $1,500): former debt plus debts incurred, less repayments, less the reduction.
-- s 140-30: cents are disregarded; under $1 is zero. s 140-25(2): the debt is incurred on 1 June. For the financial year
-- starting 1 July 2024, s 140-26(2) substitutes a formula that is also not in the deposit: not encoded.
GIVEN `former accumulated debt` IS A NUMBER, `HELP debts incurred` IS A NUMBER, `HELP debt repayments` IS A NUMBER,
      `location-preferred reduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the accumulated HELP debt` MEANS
    `the greater of` 0 (FLOOR (`former accumulated debt` PLUS `HELP debts incurred` MINUS `HELP debt repayments` MINUS `location-preferred reduction`))

§§ `ss 154-1, 154-5, 154-10, 154-15, 154-20 -- compulsory repayment`

-- s 154-5(1): repayment income is the sum of "(a) the person's taxable income for the income year, disregarding the person's
-- assessable FHSS released amount ...; (b) the person's total net investment loss ...; (c) [if an employee] the reportable fringe
-- benefits total ...; (d) the person's exempt foreign income ...; (e) the person's reportable superannuation contributions".
GIVEN `taxable income less FHSS released amount` IS A NUMBER, `total net investment loss` IS A NUMBER,
      `reportable fringe benefits total` IS A NUMBER, `exempt foreign income` IS A NUMBER,
      `reportable superannuation contributions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the repayment income` MEANS
    `taxable income less FHSS released amount` PLUS `total net investment loss` PLUS `reportable fringe benefits total`
        PLUS `exempt foreign income` PLUS `reportable superannuation contributions`

-- s 154-10: "The minimum repayment income for an income year is $67,000." s 154-20(2): 15% between the minimum and "$125,000",
-- 17% above. s 154-25(2): each is replaced by an indexed amount "At the start of each income year ... after the 2025-26 income
-- year" -- so for later years the thresholds are INPUTS.
-- INFERENCE: ss 154-10 and 154-20 were substituted ("rs No 30, 2025") by the Universities Accord (Cutting Student Debt by 20 Per
-- Cent) Act 2025, which commenced on 3 August 2025; its application provisions (Sch 2 items 33, 34) are not in the compilation.
-- Read with s 154-25(2), the compiled text speaks to the 2025-26 income year onward. Earlier years ran on the repealed text.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the stated minimum repayment income` MEANS 67000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the stated upper repayment threshold` MEANS 125000

GIVEN `income year starting in` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the compiled ss 154-10 and 154-20 speak to the income year` IF
    `income year starting in` AT LEAST 2025

-- s 154-1(1): a person is liable if "(a) the person's repayment income for an income year exceeds the minimum repayment income
-- for the income year; and (b) on 1 June immediately preceding the making of an assessment ... the person had an accumulated HELP
-- debt". (2): "not liable ... if, under section 8 of the Medicare Levy Act 1986: (a) no Medicare levy is payable by the person ...;
-- or (b) the amount of the Medicare levy payable ... is reduced."
GIVEN `repayment income` IS A NUMBER, `minimum repayment income` IS A NUMBER,
      `had an accumulated HELP debt on the preceding 1 June` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `no Medicare levy payable under s 8` IS A BOOLEAN, `Medicare levy reduced under s 8` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is liable to a compulsory repayment` IF
        `repayment income` GREATER THAN `minimum repayment income`
    AND `had an accumulated HELP debt on the preceding 1 June`
    AND (NOT `no Medicare levy payable under s 8`)
    AND (NOT `Medicare levy reduced under s 8`)

-- s 154-15(1): the repayable debt is the accumulated HELP debt, or "the amount (if any) remaining after deducting from that debt"
-- amounts paid in reduction of it or assessed under s 154-35 to be payable.
GIVEN `accumulated debt` IS A NUMBER, `amounts paid or assessed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the repayable debt` MEANS
    `the greater of` 0 (`accumulated debt` MINUS `amounts paid or assessed`)

-- s 154-20(1): the amount is "the least of the following: (a) the amount worked out under subsection (2); (b) the amount equal to
-- 10% of the person's repayment income for the income year; (c) the amount of the person's repayable debt". (2): "(a) 15% of the
-- part of the person's repayment income that exceeds the minimum repayment income but does not exceed $125,000; (b) 17% of the
-- part of the person's repayment income that exceeds $125,000."
GIVEN `repayment income` IS A NUMBER, `minimum repayment income` IS A NUMBER, `upper threshold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the marginal repayment` MEANS
        (`the greater of` 0 ((`the lesser of` `repayment income` `upper threshold`) MINUS `minimum repayment income`)) TIMES 15 DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS (`the greater of` 0 (`repayment income` MINUS `upper threshold`)) TIMES 17 DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `repayment income` IS A NUMBER, `minimum repayment income` IS A NUMBER, `upper threshold` IS A NUMBER,
      `repayable debt` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the compulsory repayment amount` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the lesser of` (`the marginal repayment` `repayment income` `minimum repayment income` `upper threshold`)
                                     (`repayment income` TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100))
                    `repayable debt`
